<section class="mb-page-head">
    <div class="container">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-crumbs">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Home</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Policies">Policies</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">Shipping &amp; refunds</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="mb-page-title">Shipping, cancellations &amp; refunds</h1>
        <p class="mb-page-text">Last updated 1 November 2026. Everything about getting a jar to you — and back.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-section mb-section-cream-2">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <div class="mb-prose">
                    <h2>Dispatch days</h2>
                    <p>
                        We pack on Mondays and Thursdays. An order paid before 10am on a packing day leaves
                        the same afternoon; anything later goes in the next one. There is no dispatch on
                        Sundays or public holidays in West Bengal.
                    </p>

                    <h2>How long it takes</h2>
                    <div class="mb-table-wrap">
                        <table class="table mb-table">
                            <caption class="visually-hidden">Delivery timelines by destination</caption>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="col">Where</th>
                                    <th scope="col">Working days</th>
                                    <th scope="col">Courier</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Kolkata, Howrah, Kharagpur</td>
                                    <td>1 – 2</td>
                                    <td>Own delivery + Delhivery</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Rest of West Bengal</td>
                                    <td>2 – 4</td>
                                    <td>Delhivery</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Metro cities (Delhi, Mumbai, Bengaluru, Chennai, Hyderabad, Pune)</td>
                                    <td>3 – 5</td>
                                    <td>Delhivery / India Post</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Rest of India</td>
                                    <td>5 – 7</td>
                                    <td>India Post (Speed Post)</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <h2>What shipping costs</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Free on orders of ₹999 and above.</li>
                        <li>A flat ₹49 below that, anywhere in India.</li>
                        <li>No hidden handling or packaging charge — the box and padding are on us.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2 id="refund">Cancellations</h2>
                    <p>
                        You can cancel any order before it is packed, free of charge. Write to us or WhatsApp
                        with the order number; the refund goes back to the same account within five working
                        days. Once a parcel is with the courier we cannot recall it, so a cancellation then
                        becomes a return.
                    </p>

                    <h2 id="returns">Returns and refunds</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Damaged in transit:</strong> send a photograph within 48 hours of delivery. We ship a replacement in the next dispatch — you do not need to return the broken jar.</li>
                        <li><strong>Wrong item sent:</strong> tell us within 48 hours; we send the correct jar and collect the wrong one.</li>
                        <li><strong>Opened food:</strong> for hygiene reasons we cannot take back a jar that has been opened, unless it is spoiled.</li>
                        <li><strong>Spoiled produce:</strong> send a photo of the jar and the batch date; a full refund is issued, no argument.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Refunds are returned to the original payment method — UPI, card or netbanking account.
                        Banks usually take three to five working days to show the credit. We do not issue
                        store credit unless you ask for it.
                    </p>

                    <h2>If a parcel goes missing</h2>
                    <p>
                        If the tracking has not moved for five working days, tell us and we will chase the
                        courier. If it is declared lost we either re-ship or refund you — your choice.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Cash on delivery</h2>
                    <p>
                        Not offered. All orders must be paid online before dispatch, which is also why every
                        parcel is insured.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <aside class="mb-note-card mb-note-card-sticky">
                    <h2 class="mb-note-title">Need to change an order?</h2>
                    <p class="mb-note-text">
                        Message us with the order number. Before packing, changes are free; after packing,
                        a return starts.
                    </p>
                    <a class="btn btn-brand btn-sm mt-2" asp-controller="Contact" asp-action="Index">Contact the farm</a>
                    <p class="mb-note-fine">Replies within one working day, usually much sooner.</p>
                </aside>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
